2	<!--
3	  chart-story: HyperFrames video primitive (proof and stats / prove)
4	
5	  One chart builds from data in reading order and lands the exact supplied
6	  values. Bars grow staggered from the baseline, a line draws left to right
7	  with an optional translucent area fill, a donut ring sweeps segment by
8	  segment, or horizontal progress bars fill top to bottom. Axis and data
9	  labels fade in reading order; the emphasized datum takes the accent color
10	  and a value callout that pops and settles on the exact value plus unit.
11	
12	  Variables:
13	    - type (bars | line | donut | progress, default "bars"): chart form.
14	    - data (string, default "12, 28, 45, 64"): comma-separated numbers.
15	    - labels (string, default "Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4"): comma-separated labels.
16	    - emphasize (number, default 3): index of the accented datum, clamped.
17	    - unit (string, default "%"): suffix appended to every value.
18	    - accent (green | blue | violet, default "green"): emphasis color.
19	    - exit (none | fade | up, default none): films end on the hold.
20	
21	  Envelope, fixed IN with elastic HOLD only (OUT exists only when exit is
22	  fade or up):
23	    IN_BASE  = 3.3s, stage arrival, axis draw, data build, labels, callout
24	    HOLD     = max(0, D - IN - OUT), one finite drift then 0.3s stillness
25	    OUT_BASE = 0.5s only when exit is fade or up, otherwise 0
26	    If D is shorter than IN_BASE + OUT_BASE, IN and OUT compress together.
27	    The timeline is never time-scaled.
28	
29	  Determinism: the whole SVG is built synchronously from the variables, all
30	  dash lengths come from getTotalLength (never the pathLength attribute, no
31	  vector-effect on dashed paths), and the callout number rows are authored
32	  frame sets, so repeated or reverse seeks always show the same pixels. The
33	  final displayed values are the raw supplied tokens, never re-rounded.
34	
35	  Mount contract: the runtime clones only this template. #root fills the host
36	  box, establishes the container query basis, has no data-width or data-height,
37	  and registers one paused timeline under the literal chart-story key.
38	-->
